PASS help :: exit 0: pc: control this PC Programs and windows pc open <link | file | folder | program> pc app <name> pc apps [filter] pc windows pc focus <title> pc close <title> pc processes [filter] pc kill <name | id> Keyboard, mouse, screen pc type <text> pc key <enter | ctrl+s | alt+f4 | win+d ...> pc click <x> <y> [right|double|triple] pc move <x> <y> pc scroll <lines> pc drag <x1> <y1> <x2> <y2> press at the first point, move, let go at the second (selects text, moves things) pc screen what the window in front shows, with the point to click for each thing pc screen ocr the same, and always reads a picture of the window too (pc screen ocr full: the whole screen) pc look <file> what is in a photo and where: the scene, each thing with its place, the writing pc look the same for the window in front as a picture (pc look full: the whole screen) pc screenshot [file.png] Sound, display, power pc volume [0-100] pc mute [on|off] pc brightness [0-100] pc say <text> pc battery pc wifi [on|off] pc info pc lock pc sleep pc shutdown [minutes] pc restart [minutes] pc cancel-shutdown pc clipboard get pc clipboard set <text> With the Termant app (it must be running) pc notify <title> [text] pc alarm <HH:MM> [label] pc timer <10m> [label] pc alarms pc alarms remove <id> pc ring [label] pc stop pc ask <question> [choices ...] waits for the answer and prints it pc rule add <at HH:MM | every 30m | startup | in 10m> do <command> pc rule list pc rule remove <id> pc note add <text> pc note list pc note remove <number> pc say <text> speaks with ElevenLabs when keys are saved (they take turns), else with the PC's own voice pc voice the ElevenLabs keys: how much each has used, which one rests pc voice add <key> [...] pc voice list (voices) pc voice use <voice id> pc voice retry Learning (with the Termant app) pc youtube search <words> videos for these words pc youtube read <id | link> [--lang hi] [--from MINUTE] what is said in a video pc skill save <name> "<what it is for>" <file with the steps> [link] pc skill list pc skill show <name> pc skill remove <name> pc learned [days] what was learned today (or in the last days) Helper agents (with the Termant app; the main agent hands them parts of a job) pc team the helpers there are pc team add <name> "<what it is for>" <file with its instructions> [provider/model] pc team show <name> pc team remove <name> Word documents (.docx; works without Word, and inside Word when the file is open there) pc word read <file> every paragraph with its number pc word new <file> [text] pc word add <file> [--bold] <text> (\n in the text starts a new paragraph) pc word replace <file> <old> <new> pc word set <file> <number> <text> pc word delete <file> <number>
